---
layout: base.njk
permalink: /research/
title: Research
description: Areas of work and open questions.
---
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="pagehead rise">
    <span class="mono">Research</span>
    <h1>Chapters, not a specialism.</h1>
    <p>Every area is dated. When the work moves on, the old chapter greys back and stays.
       Changing field means adding a chapter, not rebuilding the site.</p>
  </div>
</div>

<section class="section">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="chapters rise">
      {% for c in collections.chapters %}
      <article class="chapter" data-status="{{ c.data.status }}">
        {% if c.data.image %}<img class="chapter-img" src="{{ c.data.image }}" alt="{{ c.data.title }} research — {{ site.name }}" loading="lazy" decoding="async">{% endif %}
        <span class="chapter-span">{{ c.data.span }} · {{ c.data.status | capitalize }}</span>
        <h3>{{ c.data.title }}</h3>
        <p>{{ c.data.summary }}</p>
        <span class="chapter-meta">{{ c.data.meta }}</span>
      </article>
      {% endfor %}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="section" id="questions">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head rise"><h2>Open questions</h2></div>
    <ul class="qlist rise">
      {% for q in questions.questions %}
      <li>
        <span class="q">{{ q.text }}</span>
        <span class="q-meta">
          <span class="pill" data-state="{{ q.state }}">{% if q.state == 'open' %}Open{% elif q.state == 'active' %}In progress{% else %}Closed{% endif %}</span>
          {% if q.answer_url %}<a class="q-link" href="{{ q.answer_url }}">See the answer</a>{% endif %}
        </span>
      </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </div>
</section>
